# 1. Why Data Engineering Matters for AI Engineers

An AI application is only as reliable as the data reaching it.

```text
Source Systems
    ↓
Ingestion
    ↓
Storage
    ↓
Cleaning and Transformation
    ↓
Governance and Quality
    ↓
Features / Chunks / Embeddings
    ↓
Model, RAG System, or Agent
```

An AI engineer should understand data engineering because production AI depends on:

- Fresh data
- Correct data
- Complete data
- Authorized data
- Traceable data
- Reproducible transformations
- Scalable ingestion
- Reliable scheduling

Typical AI failures caused by data engineering issues include:

```text
Stale search index
Duplicate documents
Missing metadata
Incorrect permissions
Partial ingestion
Schema changes
Bad OCR output
Broken joins
Out-of-order streaming events
Embedding-index mismatch
```

