# 4. ETL and ELT

## 4.1 ETL

```text
Extract
Transform
Load
```

Flow:

```text
Sources
    ↓
Extract
    ↓
Transform in ETL Engine
    ↓
Load Clean Data to Target
```

Use ETL when:

- Data must be cleaned or masked before reaching the target
- The target cannot process raw data efficiently
- Legacy warehouse architecture is being used
- Strict predefined schemas are required before loading

Mental model:

```text
Clean first, store later.
```

---

## 4.2 ELT

```text
Extract
Load
Transform
```

Flow:

```text
Sources
    ↓
Extract
    ↓
Load Raw Data
    ↓
Transform Inside Lakehouse / Warehouse
```

Use ELT when:

- The target has scalable compute
- Raw data should be preserved
- Transformations may evolve
- Data must be reprocessed without re-extraction
- Multiple downstream use cases need different transformations

Mental model:

```text
Store first, clean later.
```

---

## 4.3 ETL vs ELT

| Area | ETL | ELT |
|---|---|---|
| Transformation timing | Before loading | After loading |
| Raw data retained | Not always | Usually yes |
| Flexibility | Lower | Higher |
| Reprocessing | May require re-extraction | Can rebuild from raw data |
| Common environment | Traditional warehouse | Cloud warehouse or lakehouse |
| AI suitability | Possible | Often better for diverse raw data |

Databricks Medallion Architecture usually follows an ELT-oriented pattern:

```text
Load raw data into Bronze
    ↓
Transform into Silver
    ↓
Create Gold data products
```

