# 5. Batch vs Streaming

## 5.1 Batch Processing

Batch processing handles a bounded collection of data.

Examples:

```text
Process yesterday's transactions
Index documents every night
Generate monthly report
```

Characteristics:

- Scheduled
- Clear start and end
- Higher latency accepted
- Easier to reason about

---

## 5.2 Streaming Processing

Streaming processes data continuously or incrementally as new events arrive.

Examples:

```text
Application events
IoT sensor data
Fraud alerts
Clickstream
New files appearing in storage
```

Characteristics:

- Unbounded input
- Incremental state
- Low or near-real-time latency
- Requires checkpointing and late-data handling

---

## 5.3 Micro-Batch

Micro-batch processing handles small batches repeatedly.

```text
New events
    ↓
Process every few seconds
    ↓
Update result
```

Apache Spark Structured Streaming commonly presents streaming operations using DataFrame-style APIs and incrementally updates results as data arrives.

