# 7. Medallion Architecture

## 7.1 Bronze Layer

Purpose:

```text
Preserve raw source data.
```

Characteristics:

- Minimal transformation
- Append-oriented
- Original fields retained
- Ingestion metadata added
- Rebuild source for downstream layers

Typical metadata:

```text
source_system
ingestion_timestamp
source_file
batch_id
record_hash
```

AI example:

```text
Raw PDF
Raw SharePoint metadata
Raw Salesforce export
Raw SQL extract
```

---

## 7.2 Silver Layer

Purpose:

```text
Create clean, standardized, validated, integrated data.
```

Typical transformations:

- Deduplicate
- Parse dates
- Standardize country names
- Handle missing values
- Enforce schema
- Join sources
- Apply business rules
- Quarantine invalid records

AI example:

```text
Extracted document text
Clean metadata
Normalized document types
Validated access-control fields
Document chunks
```

---

## 7.3 Gold Layer

Purpose:

```text
Create business-ready and use-case-ready data products.
```

Examples:

- Aggregated reporting table
- Feature table
- Curated AI knowledge table
- Embedding store
- Search-index export
- Executive dashboard dataset

---

## 7.4 Why Keep Bronze?

If downstream logic changes:

```text
Rebuild Silver and Gold from Bronze
```

Without Bronze, the team may need to re-extract data from source systems, which may be slow, unavailable, or changed.

