# 24. Common Data Engineering Mistakes

- Full reloads when incremental processing is possible
- No Bronze source-of-truth layer
- No deterministic primary key
- Blind append causing duplicates
- No checkpoint or watermark
- Running Python loops instead of Spark transformations
- Calling `collect()` on large datasets
- Using Python UDFs when built-in Spark functions are available
- Caching every DataFrame
- Broadcasting large tables
- Excessive repartitioning
- High-cardinality partition columns
- Thousands of tiny files
- No schema or data contracts
- No quarantine path
- No lineage or audit columns
- No source-to-target reconciliation
- Re-embedding every document on every run
- Losing source permissions before indexing

