# 26. Senior-Level Architecture Answer

> For an enterprise AI solution, I would use an ELT-oriented lakehouse architecture. Data from systems such as SharePoint, Salesforce, SQL, and APIs would be ingested incrementally into a Bronze layer, preserving raw source data and lineage. Spark and Delta Lake pipelines would validate, deduplicate, standardize, and enrich data into Silver tables. Gold data products would serve analytics, ML, and RAG use cases. Unity Catalog would govern tables, files, models, permissions, and lineage. For unstructured AI workloads, I would track document, chunk, permission, and embedding versions, then update the search index idempotently with reconciliation and observability. I would optimize Spark by controlling partitions, minimizing unnecessary shuffles, using appropriate joins, and addressing skew and small-file problems.

